{#
  What else is in this section, and what to read next.

  A section is meant to read as a finite thing a reader can work through, and a page that ends
  without saying what follows it leaves them at the back button. This block closes every prose
  page in a Docs section with the section's full contents in reading order, marking where the
  reader is, followed by an explicit next page (KI-WEBSITE-SITE-037).

  It also carries the reachability of the whole tree. `verify-reachable.ts` walks outward from
  the home page and fails the build on any page nothing links to; the Docs landing grid links
  only each section's *first* page, so without this block every page after the first would be
  orphaned. The contents list is what makes the section navigable and what makes it verifiable,
  which is the same property twice.
#}
{%- if section %}
  {%- set pages = [] %}
  {%- for item in collections.docsPages %}
    {%- if item.data.section == section %}{% set pages = (pages.push(item), pages) %}{% endif %}
  {%- endfor %}
  {%- if pages.length > 1 %}
    {%- set label = '' %}
    {%- for entry in docsSections %}{% if entry.slug == section %}{% set label = entry.title %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
    {%- set nextPage = null %}
    {%- for item in pages %}
      {%- if loop.index0 > 0 and pages[loop.index0 - 1].url == page.url %}{% set nextPage = item %}{% endif %}
    {%- endfor %}

<nav class="prose-provenance" aria-label="Section contents">

<p class="overline">{{ label }} · {{ pages.length }} pages</p>

<ol>
{%- for item in pages %}
  {%- if item.url == page.url %}
  <li><strong>{{ item.data.title }}</strong></li>
  {%- else %}
  <li><a href="{{ item.url }}">{{ item.data.title }}</a></li>
  {%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
</ol>

{%- if nextPage %}
<p>Next: <a href="{{ nextPage.url }}">{{ nextPage.data.title }}</a> →</p>
{%- else %}
<p>That is the end of this section. <a href="/docs/">Back to Docs</a> for the rest.</p>
{%- endif %}

</nav>

  {%- endif %}
{%- endif %}
